	(text "NEW FOR THIS BOARD, not copied from the reference (which has a single USB-C input wired straight to its converters).\nEach source reaches VIN through an ideal diode: LM74700-Q1 driving an N-channel MOSFET, wired as its datasheet's\ntypical application (source = ANODE = input, drain = CATHODE = VIN, EN tied to ANODE, 100 nF from VCAP to ANODE).\nThis lets the DC jack and USB-C be plugged in together, and blocks a reversed DC plug.\nLIMITS TO RESPECT: the converters' absolute maximum input is 26 V. Use 20 V or less. The TVS (SMBJ20A) only limits\nshort spikes; it clamps well above 26 V at high current, so it does not make a 24 V supply safe.\nStill to choose and check: the MOSFETs (40 V, a few milliohms), the fuse rating and the jack part number;\nthe inrush into the converters' input capacitors when USB-C power is applied; an over-voltage cut-off for field use."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c76f8de8-981d-5641-bb35-9c560b27815d")
	)
